cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository, please credit the repository and Samuel C. Lange
  (The Chinese University of Hong Kong), and cite the programs and papers for
  the lenses you use (see README.md).
type: dataset
title: "JWST lens image reduction"
abstract: >-
  James Webb Space Telescope NIRCam imaging of three galaxy-scale strong
  gravitational lenses (JVAS B1938+666 from GO 8281, and SPT0418-47 and
  SPT2147-50 from the TEMPLATES Early Release Science program), reduced from
  the uncalibrated MAST ramps into ready-to-model stamps: science images,
  noise maps, PSF kernels with uncertainty maps, and hand-drawn masks and
  hand-marked multiple-image positions, together with the pipeline that
  produces them.
authors:
  - family-names: Lange
    given-names: Samuel C.
    affiliation: The Chinese University of Hong Kong
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-0679-818X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/samlange04/JWST_lenses_data_reduction"
url: "https://github.com/samlange04/JWST_lenses_data_reduction"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - strong gravitational lensing
  - James Webb Space Telescope
  - NIRCam
  - data reduction
  - B1938+666
  - TEMPLATES
date-released: "2026-10-27"
